To create a custom memory allocator in C++ for CUDA memory operations in PyTorch, you can define the `my_malloc` and `my_free` functions as shown below. These functions should be compiled into a shared library (`.so` file) and can then be used with `torch.cuda.memory.CUDAPluggableAllocator` in Python.

```cpp
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <cuda_runtime_api.h>
#include <iostream>

extern "C" {
void* my_malloc(ssize_t size, int device, cudaStream_t stream) {
   void *ptr;
   cudaMalloc(&ptr, size);
   std::cout << "alloc " << ptr << size << std::endl;
   return ptr;
}

void my_free(void* ptr, ssize_t size, int device, cudaStream_t stream) {
   std::cout << "free " << ptr << " " << stream << std::endl;
   cudaFree(ptr);
}
}
```

Compile this code with:

```sh
g++ alloc.cc -o alloc.so -I/usr/local/cuda/include -shared -fPIC
```

In Python, you can use the shared library with `torch.cuda.memory.CUDAPluggableAllocator`.

